  "all_ingredients_flat": "zucchinis, Serrano, jalapeño, cilantro, vegetable broth, urad dal, cumin seeds, coriander seeds, mustard seeds, hing (asafetida), tamarind paste, salt, yellow moong dal, quinoa, ginger, turmeric powder, curry leaves, spinach, tomato, pickled cucumber, hot peppers, various spices",
  "instructions": "ZUCCHINI CHUTNEY: Chop 2 or 3 zucchinis into thin slices. Finely mince a hot pepper like Serrano or jalapeño. Sauté the zucchini and hot pepper (minced) with some cilantro and a dash of vegetable broth. Dry roast 1 tsp urad dal, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 tsp coriander seeds, 1 tsp mustard seeds and a pinch of hing (asafetida). Let everything cool down. Grind them together with some tamarind paste. Add some salt if using. MOONG DOSA: BATTER: Soak 2 cups yellow moong dal and 1/2 cup quinoa for 4 hours. Grind them with 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 inch ginger, 3/4 tsp turmeric powder and a handful of curry leaves (to taste). Make oil-free dosa using the batter on a non-stick pan or a cast iron tawa. MOONG DOSA WRAP: Assemble the wrap as shown in pics with Moong Dosa, spinach, tomato, pickled cucumber & Zucchini Chutney.",
